1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,989
Look at one day of gold. The morning is quiet, a small range.

2
00:00:10,439 --> 00:00:15,272
In the afternoon it suddenly speeds up. And in the evening, another big move.

3
00:00:15,722 --> 00:00:21,677
One day, three different moods. Because three different markets open in one day.

4
00:00:22,128 --> 00:00:25,054
Today we look at a separate profile for each of them.

5
00:00:26,054 --> 00:00:30,964
Hello, this is episode nine of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

6
00:00:31,415 --> 00:00:41,132
Last time: VWAP and its bands. Before that: volume profile, POC, value area.

7
00:00:41,582 --> 00:00:45,370
Today the same volume profile, but one for each session.

8
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:52,718
First, the Asia session. In India time, roughly from 5:30 in the morning to the afternoon.

9
00:00:53,168 --> 00:00:58,079
Second, London. Roughly from 1:30 in the afternoon into the night.

10
00:00:58,529 --> 00:01:04,013
Third, New York. Roughly from 6:30 in the evening until late night.

11
00:01:04,464 --> 00:01:08,905
These times shift by an hour between winter and summer.

12
00:01:09,905 --> 00:01:12,256
Each session has its own character.

13
00:01:12,705 --> 00:01:18,896
Asia is often quiet. Low volume, small range, a balanced market.

14
00:01:19,347 --> 00:01:24,493
When London opens, volume rises. The Asia range often breaks.

15
00:01:24,943 --> 00:01:31,708
New York brings the big US news. The move either continues or reverses.

16
00:01:32,708 --> 00:01:38,038
Instead of one profile for the whole day, build a separate profile for each session.

17
00:01:38,488 --> 00:01:43,399
Each gets its own POC, value area high and value area low.

18
00:01:43,848 --> 00:01:48,603
This clearly shows which session accepted which price as fair.

19
00:01:49,603 --> 00:01:55,951
Here is the real use. The previous session's profile becomes the map for the next one.

20
00:01:56,401 --> 00:02:03,166
Asia's POC, VAH and VAL act as levels in London.

21
00:02:03,616 --> 00:02:06,202
And London's levels act as levels in New York.

22
00:02:06,652 --> 00:02:10,441
The market often comes back to test these levels.

23
00:02:11,441 --> 00:02:16,847
Say London opens and price moves above the Asia value area high.

24
00:02:17,298 --> 00:02:24,376
If price holds there and volume builds above, that is acceptance, a sign to go higher.

25
00:02:24,827 --> 00:02:30,862
If price pokes above and quickly falls back into value, that is rejection.

26
00:02:31,311 --> 00:02:35,439
Then price often travels to the other edge of the value area.

27
00:02:36,439 --> 00:02:43,518
An important difference. While a session runs, its profile is still forming. That is a developing profile.

28
00:02:43,968 --> 00:02:49,454
Its POC keeps moving. Here now, somewhere else a little later.

29
00:02:49,904 --> 00:02:55,625
Once the session ends, the profile is closed. Now the levels are fixed.

30
00:02:56,075 --> 00:03:00,751
Trust a closed profile as a level, not a developing one.

31
00:03:01,751 --> 00:03:04,755
The first hour of every session is special.

32
00:03:05,204 --> 00:03:12,206
New players arrive, volume jumps, and you often get the first clue about direction.

33
00:03:12,656 --> 00:03:18,924
The first hour's high and low form a range too. Watch whether it breaks or holds.

34
00:03:19,924 --> 00:03:24,679
There is also a window when London and New York are both open.

35
00:03:25,129 --> 00:03:30,380
In India time, roughly from 6:30 to 9:30 in the evening.

36
00:03:30,829 --> 00:03:36,786
This is usually the highest-volume part of the day. Big moves often form here.

37
00:03:37,786 --> 00:03:39,430
Three common mistakes.

38
00:03:39,881 --> 00:03:44,009
One: treating a developing POC as a fixed level.

39
00:03:44,459 --> 00:03:49,291
Two: trading every session level blindly, without confirmation.

40
00:03:49,741 --> 00:03:59,146
Three: remember, in spot forex and gold, volume is only the broker's tick volume. It is an estimate, not the full picture.

41
00:04:00,146 --> 00:04:01,634
So, today's summary.

42
00:04:02,084 --> 00:04:08,275
Three sessions a day: Asia, London, New York, each with its own mood.

43
00:04:08,726 --> 00:04:17,894
The previous session's POC, VAH and VAL become levels in the next one. Watch for acceptance or rejection.

44
00:04:18,344 --> 00:04:24,300
Trust closed profiles, and watch the first hour and the overlap closely.

45
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:31,491
